														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4858696">
									

<p>So, I did a very detailed breakdown of my thoughts, but it's taking a bit to cohesively put them together, so I'll summarize:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The notes at the end are from the perspective of the Doctor who decided to enter the Time Box - the Misters being referred to are the respective computers, and the reason that this is Apollyon is because it's inevitable that any AI whose goal is to create music will replicate a specific song that matches the name of an abstract entity in deep-space, which will cause the universe to swap properties with that entity and thus become abstracted and unreal.</p>
<p>What's interesting is that he redacted everything BEFORE entering the box, and he gives his reasoning in that very first Addendum note (which happens to describe LOGICIAN from SCP-INTEGER.) That entire addendum section is being written while he's in the box, and he slowly goes insane. Before he loses everything entirely, he desperately tries to save the changes he's made&#8230; which fail because he doesn't have access privileges. Which he lost when he lost his identity in the box.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>This whole skip is a tribute to SCP-INTEGER&#8230; Placeholder's very first skip :D</p>
<p>Edit: I really like how you snuck Placeholder's name in, but I am not certain how relevant that is, other than a fun easter egg.</p>

							</div>

								
					
