<p>I remain fascinated by the &quot;possibilities&quot; of this line of thinking</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Sure, but there's no guarantee the audience will be similarly fascinated just because you are. Be careful not to confuse &quot;intellectually complicated&quot; with &quot;interesting&quot;.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I have to admit, I find this confusing. I thought D-Class came off of death row. Who goes to death row but murderers?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is a question you can answer on your own with a little research: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capital_punishment#Capital_crime">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capital_punishment#Capital_crime</a> Suffice it to say, the assumption that only murderers are put on death row would be incorrect.</p>
