<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Horror</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> ACS Header, basic layout, etc.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A user on Discord that causes a person's existence to vanish</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The person in question is called &quot;User05&quot; on Discord, and the exact name + tag is censored. The only way to come into contact with the user is pure luck. He'll usually send a friend request (which should not be accepted).</p>
<p>When a person starts talking to User05, he'll seem normal at first, seemingly like he used to know them or they used to be friends. After about ten (10) minutes of talking, stuff starts getting weird.</p>
<ul>
<li>Vagueness</li>
<li>Familiar pictures of the persons life</li>
<li>Misspelling</li>
<li>Faster typing</li>
<li>Spamming random letters</li>
</ul>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The victim might not see anything odd about it, just a casual troll on Discord. However, things get even stranger when he states the full legal name of the victim, age, and physical appearances. He sends pictures of the victim's face in various angles in random areas, as though he never knew he was being pictured. After this event, User05 goes silent for around 3-5 days.</p>
<p>After he returns, he claims that he knows where he lives, who he lives with, and will arrive there shortly. The first way of contact is through mail, which is a piece of paper that says &quot;Hi. :) - Me&quot;<br />
If the victim continues to talk to the man on Discord, the SCP will speak in an unknown language, send pictures resembling satanism practices, etc.</p>
<ul>
<li>Unknown language</li>
<li>Pictures of satanism</li>
<li>Spamming of the phrase &quot;C0N9V3RT&quot;, followed by random symbols</li>
<li>Spam calls</li>
<li>Discord crashing</li>
</ul>
<p>The victim will feel the sudden urge to block or unfriend the SCP after Discord crashes, and the urge can not be stopped no matter how much the victim denies it.</p>
<p>Blocking the SCP, or unfriending the SCP will just make things worse. If a victim does so, they will hear knocking on their front door directly after they unfriend/block User05. Their computer will crash, and all the doors in the house will lock (even if they don't have a lock on it). After the knocking stops, the door will open, and footsteps can be noticeable at this point, and get louder by the second, and faster, to the point where he's practically running. The footsteps stop at the bedroom door, but the door doesn't open. The light in the room will either explode or turn off, and the fan will turn on if it's off, or off it's it on. After the lights go out, the victim loses consciousness, and disappear out of everyone's life. However, after he goes missing, no trace of him will be left behind (SSN, birth certificate, any licenses, any proof of existence) as he just never existed in the first place. No missing posters, no sobbing relatives, nothing, he never existed.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> A cool anomaly that sort of follows the generic paranormal scheme, but it's detection is almost impossible as the victim's existence vanishes and no one knows who he is (as the people who do, don't exist).</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
