					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thedevelopingcookie" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5262630); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5262630&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609445204" alt="TheDevelopingCookie" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5262630)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thedevelopingcookie" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5262630); return false;" >TheDevelopingCookie</a></span> <span class="odate time_1609438352 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">31 Dec 2020 18:12</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-50742/per-page-discussions">Per Page Discussions / Per page discussions</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/scp-5870/comments/show">SCP-5870</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4858652">
									

<p>I didn’t say it was a joke, I said the pacing wasn’t right to me. I was surprised the ending was “just like that”, if that makes sense.</p>
<p>In my opinion, in the nicest way possible, I can see <em>you</em> on the other side of the screen, writing this. Not a foundation researcher. The writer seems passionate and excited about this topic. It can have a happy ending, but maybe have them report things as</p>
<p>“The case [of the disappearance of the many koalas] was originally thought to be a massive poaching operation that would damage the ecosystem was dismissed, but when the events’ anonymous properties became apparent research into the disappearances quickly began.”</p>
<p>For me it needs to have that sense of, ‘a sad thing is happening and we don’t give squat about it until we can prove it fits under our strict criteria.’ That’s was missing for me in this piece. Some sad moments could make the happy ending have a larger impact.</p>
<p>And about being skeptical, you can go ahead and dismiss my advice as wrong but it is advice and I think you should take it and craft this SCP to be 1% better. People generally don’t like my SCPs and I feel kinda hated on the forum but I’m trying to help people and pitch ideas that haven’t been thought of yet. I’m gonna leave it here before it turns into a rant.</p>
<p>Good luck with your article.</p>

							</div>

								
					
